          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20791 efalnd: Reference count connections",
        "message": "LU-20791 efalnd: Reference count connections\n\nConnections were destroyed by the connection daemon based only on idle\ntime and empty transmit queues. A connection could still be referenced\nby a context that had looked it up, or by an in-flight transmit that had\nnot yet completed, leaving that context to dereference freed memory.\n\nAdd a reference count to the connection. A lookup or creation returns a\nreference that the calling context owns and releases before it returns.\nA transmit takes its own reference when it adopts a connection and\nreleases it on completion.\n\nThe reference count is checked only at the final destroy step, together\nwith the existing idle time and empty queue checks. Idle time alone\ndecides when a connection enters the cleanup pipeline, so that the drain\nstage can force stuck transmits to complete and drop their references. A\ntransmit can stay outstanding until a remote reply arrives, so holding a\nconnection out of cleanup while a reference is outstanding could leave\nit alive indefinitely when that reply never comes.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nChange-Id: I54d86dd0a1156af52183497eddaa9065c93a603a\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69413\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Zanhua Huang <zanhua@amazon.com>\nReviewed-by: Michael Margolin <mrgolin@amazon.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
